<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baquates</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Baquates were a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> people of Roman Mauretania Tingitana, in present-day northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>. Altars set up at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volubilis">Volubilis</a> between the second and fourth centuries CE record agreements and renewed treaties of peace between their chiefs and Roman governors, which show how <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> managed the peoples beyond its frontier through diplomacy as well as force.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baquates.jpg" alt="Baquates" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dorieo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Latin_inscription_of_Volubilis_10.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
